W: 'Tis the gift to be sim-ple, 'tis the gift to be free; 'Tis the
W:gift to come down where we ought to be; And
W:when we find our-selves in the place just right, 'Twill
W:be in the val-ley of love and de-light.
W:When true simplic-i-ty is gain'd,
W:To bow and to bend we shan't be a-shame'd
W: To turn, turn will be our de-light, 'Till by
W:turn-ing, turn-ing we come round right.
